  day: [["7:30 AM", "Review dispatch: two no-cool calls, one maintenance agreement and a heat pump install."], ["8:15 AM", "Diagnose a no-cool call: the outdoor unit hums but the fan won’t start: test and replace a failed run capacitor."], ["10:00 AM", "Perform spring maintenance: clean the condenser coil, check electrical connections and measure superheat."], ["12:30 PM", "Join the install crew to set a new heat pump, braze line sets and pull a vacuum to 500 microns."], ["3:00 PM", "Start up the new system, verify charge by subcooling and measure static pressure."], ["4:30 PM", "Walk the homeowner through the thermostat and filter schedule and complete paperwork."]],
  env: "HVAC technicians work in homes, offices, schools, hospitals, factories and stores. Work can be in attics, crawlspaces, rooftops and mechanical rooms, in extreme heat or cold. Hazards include electrical shock, burns, refrigerants and falls.",
  schedule: "Mostly full-time, with heavy overtime in peak summer and winter seasons. Many techs take rotating on-call shifts for emergencies.",
