  iq: [["Which welding processes are you comfortable with?", "List processes and positions honestly, and offer to take a weld test."], ["How do you prevent porosity?", "Mention cleaning base metal, proper gas flow, avoiding drafts and checking for leaks."], ["Can you read weld symbols?", "Explain the basics: arrow side versus other side, weld type, size and length."], ["Tell me about a time you had to fix a bad weld.", "Describe finding the defect, grinding it out and rewelding correctly."], ["What PPE do you use?", "List helmet, safety glasses, gloves, FR clothing, boots and respiratory protection when needed."]],
  faq: [["How long does it take to become a welder?", "Many technical programs take several months to two years. Some welders start as helpers and learn on the job, then pass employer weld tests."], ["Do welders need certification?", "Not legally in most cases, but employers commonly require you to pass a weld test to their procedure or hold AWS certification."], ["What kind of welder earns the most?", "Specialists such as pipe welders, underwater welders and those in energy or aerospace often earn the most, especially with overtime and travel."]],
  quiz: [["Which process uses a continuously fed wire and shielding gas?", ["SMAW", "GMAW (MIG)", "Oxy-fuel", "Brazing"], 1, "MIG welding feeds wire continuously with shielding gas."], ["Pinholes on a weld surface are called:", ["Undercut", "Porosity", "Slag", "Overlap"], 1, "Porosity comes from trapped gas."], ["What does 1G refer to?", ["A flat groove weld", "Vertical fillet", "Overhead groove", "Fixed pipe at 45 degrees"], 0, "1G is the flat groove position."], ["Why use preheat on some metals?", ["To clean paint", "To reduce the risk of cracking", "To speed up cooling", "To save gas"], 1, "Preheat slows cooling and reduces cracking."], ["A hot work permit is needed to:", ["Weld in areas with fire risk", "Buy a welder", "Use a grinder at home", "Drive a forklift"], 0, "Hot work permits control fire hazards."]],
  path: [["Welder Helper", "Prepare materials and assist welders."], ["Certified Welder", "Weld to codes and procedures."], ["Specialist or Lead Welder", "Pipe, structural or TIG specialist, or shop lead."], ["Welding Inspector (CWI) or Supervisor", "Inspect, train or manage fabrication."]],
